course: dictionary
lesson: 3592
title: Fidgety and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fidgety means unable to keep still. Your hands tap, your feet wriggle, and your body keeps shifting. «Sam was fidgety all through the long assembly, swinging his legs and tapping his pencil.» The clues are long assembly and swinging legs, so fidgety must mean wriggling and not able to sit still.
explain: Feelings are clues too. «Maya got fidgety in the car, asking how much longer until we arrived.» Nobody is angry or hurt here. She just cannot settle, so fidgety can show boredom or nerves. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Maya got unable to keep still in the car" still makes sense.
explain: Words from other languages work the same way. In a Chinese story, «nǐ zhēn hóu!» teases a cheeky, fidgety kid, and hóuzi means monkey. Fidget is also a noun: a fidget toy is a small toy for busy hands.
fact: Fidgety means unable to keep still, moving your hands, feet or body a lot.
fact: Fidgety can show you are bored, nervous or restless.
fact: A fidget toy is a small toy for busy hands.
fact: «Stop fidgeting» means keep still.
fact: Fidgety, fidgetier and fidgetiest compare how much someone wriggles, from a little to the most.
exercise: «Sam was fidgety all through the long assembly, swinging his legs.» What does fidgety mean? | Happy and singing loudly | Holding a book very carefully | Fast asleep in his chair | *Unable to keep still
exercise: Priya says a fidget toy is a big, loud drum. What is a fidget toy really? | *A small toy for busy hands | A game played on a computer | A big drum for the school band | A toy that is very quiet and still
exercise: «Maya got fidgety in the car, asking how much longer.» What feeling does fidgety suggest here? | Proud and famous | Sick and dizzy | *Bored or restless, not able to settle | Calm and content
test: What does «stop fidgeting» ask a child to do? | Dance | Shout loudly | *Keep still | Run away
test: Which word means the most wriggly of all? | *fidgetiest | fidgety | fidgetier | fidget
exam: Which sentence uses fidgety correctly? | *The fidgety puppy could not stay still on the mat. | The cat sat still on the warm mat. | Fidgety is a loud drum played in the band. | The fidget was asleep in the bed.
